# custom.rules.example — template for user-defined audit checks.
#
# Copy this file to custom.rules and edit it. `mb audit run` will pick up
# custom.rules automatically and run any check_<key> function defined in
# modules/cis-benchmark.sh that matches a key below.
#
# Format:
#   <key>=<expected_value>
#
# Keys are free-form. Each key is matched against the output of a function
# named `check_custom_<key>` (case-insensitive). If no matching function
# exists, the key is reported as WARN with a hint to define the function.
#
# Example entries (uncomment and edit):

# MyServiceRunning=yes
# MyServiceEnabled=yes
# DataDirPerms=750
# CustomBannerSet=yes
